  "preconditions": [
    "12.r.W: A validated stored line_range with explicit encoding, 1-based inclusive start/end and expected selection SHA-256; read_code_reference supplies an owned file or historical Git source snapshot.",
    "12.r.R: read_code_reference supplies a bound immutable source; line_range uses required H.2 fields, text_anchor evaluation requires explicit code-anchor-v1 text/bytes coordinates. Legacy anchors remain stored unchanged and are not inferred."
  ],
  "steps": [
    "Validate required stored range fields; strictly decode original source bytes in the stored encoding, normalize CRLF and CR to LF, select exactly the inclusive stored lines including their existing LF terminators, then compare SHA-256 over UTF-8 selection bytes. Check other Unicode separators and decomposed text remain unchanged, outside modifications do not change a matching selection, and wrong expected hashes are not accepted because the raw file hash matches. Reject unavailable ranges and encoding failures without truncation or replacement. Compare file/historical Git results and unchanged source data; exercise detached values and fresh standard-library-only Core/PYZ processes without I/O, execution or writes during selection.",
    "Check the complete stored window first; otherwise hash all complete windows of the declared line/byte extent, including overlapping positions. Accept only one other match as relocated; report none versus multiple separately, with no saved position changes. Exercise normalized text, original bytes, final-newline sensitivity, missing/truncated old ranges, missing/invalid encoding, unknown and conflicting anchor profiles, detached values, historical Git parity and guarded fresh Core/PYZ runtimes."
  ],
  "oracle": {
    "kind": "behavior",
    "requirement_contract": "Eine textbasierte Bereichsreferenz MUSS zusätzlich Encoding, Start-/Endzeile beziehungsweise erwartete Zeilenanzahl und Auswahlhash nach Anhang H speichern.",
    "scope": "12.r.W/R supply inclusive H.2 selection and exact location evidence: stored_position takes precedence, exactly one different complete window yields relocated, zero or multiple yield selection_missing/selection_ambiguous without a preferred position. Text is strictly decoded and CRLF/CR normalized to LF; byte anchors explicitly select unchanged bytes. Existing arbitrary anchor data remain readable but unsupported for evaluation without code-anchor-v1; no migration or guessed encoding. Source and reference bytes remain unchanged. H.3 reference-state composition and consumers remain later steps; no full-suite or release pass is claimed."
  },
